In the current TG, "CheckConsecutiveLetters" should run when the string length is exactly 3 characters. Since the condition for a string to be happy includes both having a length of at least 3 and having distinct consecutive letters, we need to ensure that "CheckConsecutiveLetters" runs when the string length is exactly 3 to check the distinctness of its three characters.

To handle this scenario explicitly, you could modify the TG orders as follows:

```json
{
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "CheckStringLength",
            "to": "CheckConsecutiveLetters"
        },
        {
            "condition": "failure",
            "from": "CheckStringLength",
            "to": "End"
        },
        {
            "condition": "length_is_exactly_3",
            "from": "CheckStringLength",
            "to": "CheckConsecutiveLetters"
        }
    ]
}
```

This way, if the string length is exactly 3 characters, it will directly proceed to check for consecutive distinct letters.
